WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.205 --> 00:00:01.413
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:04.758
We put out a ton of top 10
rules for success this year.

00:00:04.758 --> 00:00:06.788
It's been an amazing year, tons of fun,

00:00:06.788 --> 00:00:08.791
tons of motivation and inspiration.

00:00:08.791 --> 00:00:12.210
I thought what a cool idea it
might be to end off this year,

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:16.554
is to share some of my favorite
top 10 rules for success,

00:00:16.554 --> 00:00:19.923
that were all produced in 2016,

00:00:19.923 --> 00:00:22.706
to give you guys one last clip to watch,

00:00:22.706 --> 00:00:27.437
one last jump of inspiration
to go into 2017 strong.

00:00:27.437 --> 00:00:28.854
I hope you enjoy.

00:00:31.593 --> 00:00:34.687
- My assistant's got a
great thing now and it's ...

00:00:34.687 --> 00:00:37.198
Once in every four months,
somebody sends an email saying,

00:00:37.198 --> 00:00:40.126
"I've got a huge startup
that I want you to invest in,

00:00:40.126 --> 00:00:43.248
but you've got to sign this NDA," right,

00:00:43.248 --> 00:00:45.178
which literally every
time gets an email back

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.487
that says, "F**k you."

00:00:47.487 --> 00:00:52.131
The reason is, I'm a humongous
believer that ideas are s**t

00:00:52.131 --> 00:00:54.209
and that execution is the game.

00:00:54.209 --> 00:00:55.474
We've all got ideas.

00:00:55.474 --> 00:00:57.029
Everybody's got ideas.

00:00:57.029 --> 00:00:59.120
Do you know how many f**king
ideas we all have here?

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.173
We could probably sit here
for the next two hours,

00:01:01.173 --> 00:01:02.695
draw them all out, record them,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.005
and predict the next 78 great startups

00:01:05.005 --> 00:01:06.947
over the next nine years.

00:01:06.947 --> 00:01:07.780
And...

00:01:08.703 --> 00:01:13.699
I think the thing that is
another theme in entrepreneurship

00:01:13.699 --> 00:01:18.312
is there is way too much
fodder brought to the idea ...

00:01:18.312 --> 00:01:21.645
Uber was Magic Cab three years earlier.

00:01:21.645 --> 00:01:22.832
Uber's not an idea.

00:01:22.832 --> 00:01:23.735
Uber existed.

00:01:23.735 --> 00:01:25.363
It was called Magic Cab,

00:01:25.363 --> 00:01:29.388
but the guys that executed
it, sucked, so they lost.

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:33.454
I think, if there's any level
of romance left in this room

00:01:33.454 --> 00:01:36.113
about your idea, I'd like to suffocate it,

00:01:36.113 --> 00:01:38.294
because I think the actual situation

00:01:38.294 --> 00:01:40.527
is what you actually do with it.

00:01:40.527 --> 00:01:44.829
- I talk to so many smart,
fantastic, ambitious, idealistic,

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:47.999
hard-working kids and
they're right out of college

00:01:47.999 --> 00:01:50.267
in their entry level
jobs and I'll ask them,

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.777
"How's it going?"

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:54.807
They'll say, "I think I'm going to quit."

00:01:54.807 --> 00:01:56.596
I'm like, "Why?"

00:01:56.596 --> 00:01:59.697
They say to me, "I'm
not making an impact."

00:01:59.697 --> 00:02:02.024
I'm like, "You know you've
been here eight months, right?"

00:02:02.024 --> 00:02:04.428
(laughter)

00:02:04.428 --> 00:02:08.029
They treat the sense of
fulfillment, or even love,

00:02:08.029 --> 00:02:09.576
like it's a scavenger hunt,

00:02:09.576 --> 00:02:11.645
like it's something you look for.

00:02:11.645 --> 00:02:14.338
My millennial friends, they've
gone through so many jobs.

00:02:14.338 --> 00:02:16.989
They're either getting
fired, I mean, it was mutual.

00:02:16.989 --> 00:02:19.799
(laughter)

00:02:19.799 --> 00:02:22.760
Or they're quitting because
they're not making an impact

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.268
or they're not finding the
thing they're looking for.

00:02:24.268 --> 00:02:25.634
They're not feeling fulfilled.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.293
As if it's a scavenger hunt.

00:02:27.293 --> 00:02:28.126
Love,

00:02:29.002 --> 00:02:31.002
a job you find joy from,

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:34.400
is not something you discover.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.595
It's not like I found love.

00:02:36.595 --> 00:02:37.561
Here it is.

00:02:37.561 --> 00:02:39.093
I found a job I love.

00:02:39.093 --> 00:02:40.737
That's not how it works.

00:02:40.737 --> 00:02:42.636
Both of those things require hard work.

00:02:42.636 --> 00:02:45.018
You are in love because you work very hard

00:02:45.018 --> 00:02:49.423
every single day of your
life to stay in love.

00:02:49.423 --> 00:02:52.017
You find a job that
brings you ultimate joy

00:02:52.017 --> 00:02:54.944
because you work hard every single day

00:02:54.944 --> 00:02:58.051
to serve those around you
and you maintain that joy.

00:02:58.051 --> 00:03:00.165
It's not a discovery.

00:03:00.165 --> 00:03:03.280
The problem is the sense of impatience.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.992
It's as if an entire
generation is standing

00:03:04.992 --> 00:03:05.951
at the foot of a mountain.

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:07.892
They know exactly what they want.

00:03:07.892 --> 00:03:08.766
They can see the summit.

00:03:08.766 --> 00:03:10.646
What they can't see is the mountain,

00:03:10.646 --> 00:03:13.063
this large, immovable object.

00:03:14.619 --> 00:03:16.077
That doesn't mean you
have to do your time.

00:03:16.077 --> 00:03:17.918
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:03:17.918 --> 00:03:20.037
Take a helicopter, climb, I don't care.

00:03:20.037 --> 00:03:22.106
There's still a mountain.

00:03:22.106 --> 00:03:27.039
Life, career fulfillment,
relationships, are journeys.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:29.352
The problem is, this entire generation

00:03:29.352 --> 00:03:32.086
has an institutionalized
sense of impatience.

00:03:32.086 --> 00:03:34.760
Do they have the patience
to go on the journey

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.819
to maintain love, to feel fulfilled,

00:03:37.819 --> 00:03:39.403
or do they just quit and on to the next,

00:03:39.403 --> 00:03:41.278
dump and on to the next,

00:03:41.278 --> 00:03:43.477
ghost and on to the next?

00:03:43.477 --> 00:03:46.341
- When I was about eight years old,

00:03:46.341 --> 00:03:48.927
I grew up in the church

00:03:48.927 --> 00:03:52.844
and I was going to one
of those women's day ...

00:03:53.842 --> 00:03:57.259
You know how we have church all day long.

00:03:58.781 --> 00:04:01.668
I'd been to Sunday School
and we were going to ...

00:04:01.668 --> 00:04:04.184
Then afternoon, they were
having a women's tea,

00:04:04.184 --> 00:04:05.984
from the Women's Board.

00:04:05.984 --> 00:04:08.218
They were having a tea and the
little girl that was supposed

00:04:08.218 --> 00:04:11.885
to be there to do
recitation had gotten ill.

00:04:12.929 --> 00:04:17.419
They said to my stepmother,
"We need a little girl.

00:04:17.419 --> 00:04:20.726
Can Oprah come back and do a
recitation this afternoon?"

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:21.983
My stepmother said, "Yeah,

00:04:21.983 --> 00:04:24.102
I'll have her back here this afternoon."

00:04:24.102 --> 00:04:27.306
You know church ain't over 'til 1:30.

00:04:27.306 --> 00:04:30.973
By four o'clock, I had
gone home and learned

00:04:32.099 --> 00:04:35.766
to recite Invictus by
William Ernest Henley.

00:04:36.845 --> 00:04:40.647
Now, it starts out, "Out of
the night that covers me,

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:42.800
Black as the pit from pole to pole,

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.035
I thank whatever gods may be,

00:04:45.035 --> 00:04:46.770
For my unconquerable soul."

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:50.687
I was reciting it and doing
the pit from pole to pole.

00:04:50.687 --> 00:04:53.539
I didn't know what I was saying.

00:04:53.539 --> 00:04:57.721
At the end of the poem, there
is the stanza that says,

00:04:57.721 --> 00:05:01.522
"It matters not how strait the gate,

00:05:01.522 --> 00:05:04.682
How charged with punishment the scroll,

00:05:04.682 --> 00:05:06.932
I am the master of my fate,

00:05:09.682 --> 00:05:12.099
I am the captain of my soul."

00:05:12.962 --> 00:05:15.594
Now my little eight year
old brain didn't really

00:05:15.594 --> 00:05:19.734
fully understand the power
and depth of those words,

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:22.521
but they sounded good enough
for me to write them down

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:24.372
and put them on my mirror.

00:05:24.372 --> 00:05:27.789
Those words, "I am the master of my fate,

00:05:29.042 --> 00:05:33.295
I am the captain of my soul,"
became a mantra for me.

00:05:33.295 --> 00:05:35.962
What it said is I am responsible

00:05:36.938 --> 00:05:40.458
for the choices that I make in my life.

00:05:40.458 --> 00:05:41.875
I am responsible.

00:05:43.882 --> 00:05:45.299
I am responsible.

00:05:46.663 --> 00:05:49.827
Obviously, I grew up and was better able

00:05:49.827 --> 00:05:53.638
to articulate what
those words really mean.

00:05:53.638 --> 00:05:55.832
I discovered in physics class ...

00:05:55.832 --> 00:05:58.890
Those of you who remember physics ...

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:01.909
The third law of motion, do
you remember what that is?

00:06:01.909 --> 00:06:04.426
The third law of motion in physics says,

00:06:04.426 --> 00:06:05.544
"For every action ...

00:06:05.544 --> 00:06:10.323
It's called Newton's Law, and
it says, "For every action,

00:06:10.323 --> 00:06:13.740
there is an equal and opposite reaction."

00:06:14.952 --> 00:06:15.906
What does that mean?

00:06:15.906 --> 00:06:18.852
That means everything
that you are putting out

00:06:18.852 --> 00:06:21.685
into the world, every action, bam,

00:06:22.769 --> 00:06:26.185
there is an equal and opposite reaction.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:31.070
It means no matter what you
do, the energy of what you do,

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:35.745
what you say, and most important,
the energy of who you are,

00:06:35.745 --> 00:06:40.129
is going out into the
world, into your home,

00:06:40.129 --> 00:06:42.444
into your relationships,

00:06:42.444 --> 00:06:46.194
and that energy is always
coming back to you.

00:06:47.903 --> 00:06:51.369
You are responsible for the
energy that you are putting out

00:06:51.369 --> 00:06:55.332
into the world, 'cuz
that very energy, bam,

00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:58.501
is coming right back to
you, every single time,

00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:01.828
whether you believe it
or not, 'cuz it is law.

00:07:01.828 --> 00:07:03.227
It is law.

00:07:03.227 --> 00:07:05.837
It is law that what you put out

00:07:05.837 --> 00:07:07.933
into the world is coming back.

00:07:07.933 --> 00:07:12.100
- If you're good at what you
do, people will recognize that.

00:07:13.797 --> 00:07:15.365
I really believe it.

00:07:15.365 --> 00:07:19.546
I really believe that going
out and playing good songs,

00:07:19.546 --> 00:07:23.713
live, as a great live band,
will make you successful.

00:07:25.381 --> 00:07:26.783
I really think it will.

00:07:26.783 --> 00:07:30.027
It doesn't matter if you're at
the s**thole down the street

00:07:30.027 --> 00:07:32.171
or you're on the side stage at Bonnaroo,

00:07:32.171 --> 00:07:33.862
or you're headlining Lollapalooza.

00:07:33.862 --> 00:07:37.034
If you're a great band with great songs,

00:07:37.034 --> 00:07:39.136
people will notice it.

00:07:39.136 --> 00:07:40.265
That's it.

00:07:40.265 --> 00:07:41.635
That's all it is.

00:07:41.635 --> 00:07:43.436
It's that simple.

00:07:43.436 --> 00:07:47.436
F**k product placement
and labels and A&amp;R people

00:07:50.308 --> 00:07:52.106
and all that bulls**t.

00:07:52.106 --> 00:07:54.574
It doesn't f**king matter.

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:55.993
I swear to God.

00:07:55.993 --> 00:07:58.032
It doesn't matter.

00:07:58.032 --> 00:08:00.126
If you back that up with the idea

00:08:00.126 --> 00:08:05.050
that just playing those great
songs in your great live band

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:09.823
is enough reward for you,
then you're f**king set.

00:08:09.823 --> 00:08:11.732
But you've got to be bad ass.

00:08:11.732 --> 00:08:14.684
You just have to be really good.

00:08:14.684 --> 00:08:15.596
It's the other things

00:08:15.596 --> 00:08:19.213
that make up for your musical inability.

00:08:19.213 --> 00:08:20.046
You know?

00:08:20.046 --> 00:08:23.296
I mean, as a drummer, I never felt like

00:08:26.773 --> 00:08:29.025
I'm going to be on the cover
of Modern Drummer magazine,

00:08:29.025 --> 00:08:31.794
because I'm the best f**king
drummer in the world.

00:08:31.794 --> 00:08:34.822
I just knew that if you put me on stage,

00:08:34.822 --> 00:08:39.630
without a f**king PA or floor
monitors, in a small club,

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.930
that I would beat the
f**king s**t out of my drums

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:43.040
so much that people would go,

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:47.737
"God damn, did you see that
f**king drummer? Whoa."

00:08:47.737 --> 00:08:50.606
And I'd walk away from every
show like there you go.

00:08:50.606 --> 00:08:53.280
I just beat the f**king
piss out of those things

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.642
and people saw it.

00:08:54.642 --> 00:08:56.378
- People took notice, for sure.

00:08:56.378 --> 00:08:57.402
- And that was great.

00:08:57.402 --> 00:09:00.194
So, at the end of the show,
I was a successful musician,

00:09:00.194 --> 00:09:03.834
because I had achieved
what I wanted to achieve.

00:09:03.834 --> 00:09:04.908
I honestly believe ...

00:09:04.908 --> 00:09:06.974
I mean, I know lots of
musicians that went down

00:09:06.974 --> 00:09:08.347
to South by Southwest and said,

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:10.315
"Well, it's easy for you to say."

00:09:10.315 --> 00:09:11.816
I'm like, "Man, I was in
the same f**king position

00:09:11.816 --> 00:09:13.983
you are in, 24 years ago."

00:09:16.171 --> 00:09:17.004
That was it.

00:09:17.004 --> 00:09:18.472
I worked in a f**king furniture warehouse

00:09:18.472 --> 00:09:20.254
and I wanted people to like my music,

00:09:20.254 --> 00:09:23.985
so I played out as much
as I could, you know?

00:09:23.985 --> 00:09:26.249
If you really, honestly, like I said,

00:09:26.249 --> 00:09:30.155
if you're passionate and driven
and focused in what you do,

00:09:30.155 --> 00:09:31.992
if you're really f**king good at it,

00:09:31.992 --> 00:09:34.307
people will take notice.

00:09:34.307 --> 00:09:36.516
That's basically it.

00:09:36.516 --> 00:09:38.354
I don't understand the industry.

00:09:38.354 --> 00:09:41.957
I don't understand where music is headed.

00:09:41.957 --> 00:09:44.951
I don't really understand technology.

00:09:44.951 --> 00:09:48.451
I just know that when you walk into a club

00:09:49.328 --> 00:09:52.109
and you see a band that blows you away,

00:09:52.109 --> 00:09:54.263
you are going to follow that band.

00:09:54.263 --> 00:09:56.036
You're going to either buy their CD,

00:09:56.036 --> 00:09:57.382
or you're going to find them online,

00:09:57.382 --> 00:10:01.387
or you're going to see them the
next time they come to play.

00:10:01.387 --> 00:10:03.137
That's what it takes.

00:10:04.273 --> 00:10:07.418
You don't have to stand in
line at the song contest on TV

00:10:07.418 --> 00:10:10.950
to become a f**king popular musician,

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.249
to stand in front of some judge

00:10:12.249 --> 00:10:14.118
that doesn't even f**king
play an instrument

00:10:14.118 --> 00:10:15.867
on their own God damn records.

00:10:15.867 --> 00:10:17.654
Tell you, no, you're not good enough.

00:10:17.654 --> 00:10:20.153
- [Interviewer] Right.
- F**k that.

00:10:20.153 --> 00:10:22.986
Go blow people away in their face.

00:10:27.467 --> 00:10:29.969
I honestly believe it's that simple.

00:10:29.969 --> 00:10:31.768
- I got a ...

00:10:31.768 --> 00:10:34.028
I started working at this video store,

00:10:34.028 --> 00:10:36.220
is pretty much what you're
talking about, around that time,

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.310
and it was great at first.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:40.912
I'd always hated day jobs and stuff.

00:10:40.912 --> 00:10:43.856
I got a day job and it
ended up being pretty good.

00:10:43.856 --> 00:10:45.639
Admittedly, I was there for five years.

00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:48.302
At a certain point it was
a narcotic, all right?

00:10:48.302 --> 00:10:50.298
I didn't have to keep pursuing my dreams.

00:10:50.298 --> 00:10:53.040
You know, it's not what I want to do,

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.514
but it's sort of, kind of close.

00:10:56.514 --> 00:10:59.315
If I didn't have an
artist's soul burning in me,

00:10:59.315 --> 00:11:02.732
I could have made myself happy with that.

00:11:02.732 --> 00:11:06.411
If I didn't have an artist's
soul burning to get out,

00:11:06.411 --> 00:11:09.792
I could have walked
backwards a couple steps

00:11:09.792 --> 00:11:12.356
and just done that, and it
would have been a fulfilling,

00:11:12.356 --> 00:11:14.648
well to anybody else it would
have been a fulfilling life.

00:11:14.648 --> 00:11:15.621
It wouldn't have been for me,

00:11:15.621 --> 00:11:16.949
because I would have known
I had something to say

00:11:16.949 --> 00:11:19.149
that I didn't get a chance to say.

00:11:19.149 --> 00:11:22.951
But it did put me to sleep for a while.

00:11:22.951 --> 00:11:24.325
I've always just thought ...

00:11:24.325 --> 00:11:27.359
What really got everything
kind of truly going for me ...

00:11:27.359 --> 00:11:28.758
You could point out a
lot of different things,

00:11:28.758 --> 00:11:32.223
but the bottom line is
the fact that I realized

00:11:32.223 --> 00:11:36.079
that even the group of
people I hung around with,

00:11:36.079 --> 00:11:39.472
they were all great fellas and great gals,

00:11:39.472 --> 00:11:43.519
but it was easy for me to
think that I was doing a lot

00:11:43.519 --> 00:11:45.560
because I was doing more to try

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:48.727
to move myself forward than they were.

00:11:49.743 --> 00:11:50.955
That's not ...

00:11:50.955 --> 00:11:53.576
Okay, I'm a big fish in a puddle.

00:11:53.576 --> 00:11:54.647
So what?

00:11:54.647 --> 00:11:56.976
They're not doing anything.

00:11:56.976 --> 00:12:00.181
Yeah, I'm doing more than them.

00:12:00.181 --> 00:12:04.533
I realized that actually
I need to get my ass out

00:12:04.533 --> 00:12:08.700
to Hollywood and meet other
people who are in my category

00:12:09.548 --> 00:12:12.054
or working a little higher.

00:12:12.054 --> 00:12:15.123
I should be the weakest link in my chain

00:12:15.123 --> 00:12:17.318
that I have and that'll
make me be stronger.

00:12:17.318 --> 00:12:18.261
It'll make me run faster.

00:12:18.261 --> 00:12:21.649
I mean, like an analogy
I've always used is

00:12:21.649 --> 00:12:24.672
if you run the hundred yard dash,

00:12:24.672 --> 00:12:26.727
with people that can't run as fast as you,

00:12:26.727 --> 00:12:28.495
yeah, you'll win, hands down.

00:12:28.495 --> 00:12:29.328
You know that.

00:12:29.328 --> 00:12:32.514
But if you run with people
much faster than you,

00:12:32.514 --> 00:12:34.523
you might come in last, every single time,

00:12:34.523 --> 00:12:37.414
but your time will be better,

00:12:37.414 --> 00:12:39.824
because they're making
you run all the faster.

00:12:39.824 --> 00:12:43.237
They're making you dig down
just a little bit more.

00:12:43.237 --> 00:12:44.083
It doesn't matter that you won.

00:12:44.083 --> 00:12:45.574
Your time is faster.

00:12:45.574 --> 00:12:46.913
That's what I knew I had to do.

00:12:46.913 --> 00:12:48.708
I had to get out of Loserville

00:12:48.708 --> 00:12:51.359
and throw myself into a place where,

00:12:51.359 --> 00:12:53.760
this is what folks do for a living.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:54.981
- [Interviewer] Did you ever have,

00:12:54.981 --> 00:12:58.983
let's call it a normal
job, Conor, a nine to five?

00:12:58.983 --> 00:13:01.256
- Yeah, 'cuz the Irish thing is to get

00:13:01.256 --> 00:13:02.435
into a trade straight away.

00:13:02.435 --> 00:13:03.268
I was no different.

00:13:03.268 --> 00:13:05.931
Soon as I finished school,

00:13:05.931 --> 00:13:06.935
I was always getting pestered,

00:13:06.935 --> 00:13:10.842
"What are you doing with your
life? Doing this, doing that."

00:13:10.842 --> 00:13:11.761
They didn't know what it was.

00:13:11.761 --> 00:13:13.604
They didn't know what MMA was.

00:13:13.604 --> 00:13:14.617
They didn't know what none of this.

00:13:14.617 --> 00:13:15.714
They didn't know I could
make a career out of it.

00:13:15.714 --> 00:13:16.947
As far as they were
concerned, me ma and da,

00:13:16.947 --> 00:13:18.151
I'm talking about, as far
as they were concerned,

00:13:18.151 --> 00:13:19.082
I was just getting into a cage

00:13:19.082 --> 00:13:20.495
and fighting with some other guy.

00:13:20.495 --> 00:13:21.634
They didn't know nothing about it.

00:13:21.634 --> 00:13:22.995
No one did, really.

00:13:22.995 --> 00:13:24.119
But I knew.

00:13:24.119 --> 00:13:24.952
I knew.

00:13:26.006 --> 00:13:27.316
And then I ended up getting a trade,

00:13:27.316 --> 00:13:28.769
just to keep them quiet.

00:13:28.769 --> 00:13:30.655
'Cuz I always used to have a
lot of fights with me da, a ...

00:13:30.655 --> 00:13:31.565
- [Interviewer] What trade did you get?

00:13:31.565 --> 00:13:34.738
- I ended up getting a trade as a plumber.

00:13:34.738 --> 00:13:37.011
Literally up in the back roads an hour,

00:13:37.011 --> 00:13:38.209
up in the Wicklow Mountains.

00:13:38.209 --> 00:13:39.632
I feel like that sight was one

00:13:39.632 --> 00:13:41.885
of the biggest sights in Europe.

00:13:41.885 --> 00:13:45.187
Kilternan is right at
that skiing place, Ewich,

00:13:45.187 --> 00:13:46.419
and now it's just abandoned.

00:13:46.419 --> 00:13:47.597
Now it's just deserted.

00:13:47.597 --> 00:13:48.732
I used to go up there, six o'clock,

00:13:48.732 --> 00:13:51.185
five o'clock in the
morning, I was on the M50.

00:13:51.185 --> 00:13:53.388
I used to have to walk to the M4,

00:13:53.388 --> 00:13:54.352
about half an hour from me house

00:13:54.352 --> 00:13:55.920
and wait for some Limerick
guy that I didn't even know.

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:58.731
He drove on the M4 and
I had to flag him down.

00:13:58.731 --> 00:13:59.564
Nightmare.

00:13:59.564 --> 00:14:01.897
You have two hours down on
the M50, two hours back.

00:14:01.897 --> 00:14:04.110
Usually 14 hour days and
I was the first year,

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:04.943
so I was the ...

00:14:04.943 --> 00:14:05.915
I had to go and do everything.

00:14:05.915 --> 00:14:06.748
I had to go up to the shop.

00:14:06.748 --> 00:14:08.885
I had to go and get this and get that.

00:14:08.885 --> 00:14:10.141
I always had trouble
with that and I was like,

00:14:10.141 --> 00:14:11.181
"This isn't for me.

00:14:11.181 --> 00:14:12.132
This is not for me."

00:14:12.132 --> 00:14:13.652
- [Interviewer] How long did you last?

00:14:13.652 --> 00:14:15.975
- I lasted 18 months still.

00:14:15.975 --> 00:14:17.392
But it was tough.

00:14:18.483 --> 00:14:20.014
It wasn't the life for
me, you know what I mean?

00:14:20.014 --> 00:14:21.954
Then John said, 'cuz I
was training with John,

00:14:21.954 --> 00:14:23.512
as well, at the time.

00:14:23.512 --> 00:14:25.685
Then John got on twitch
and says, "I have a show.

00:14:25.685 --> 00:14:26.518
I'm running the show.

00:14:26.518 --> 00:14:27.594
Would you like to fight in it?"

00:14:27.594 --> 00:14:28.474
Then that was it.

00:14:28.474 --> 00:14:30.435
I just packed it in, didn't show up.

00:14:30.435 --> 00:14:31.849
Me da used to come in and
punch the hell out of me,

00:14:31.849 --> 00:14:34.814
like try to drag me out of
bed and I just wouldn't go.

00:14:34.814 --> 00:14:39.783
Then I had operal for a good
few years, when I'm overable.

00:14:39.783 --> 00:14:40.616
That was it.

00:14:40.616 --> 00:14:43.873
I just packed it in, quit,
and then focused on training.

00:14:43.873 --> 00:14:45.019
I knew what was going to happen.

00:14:45.019 --> 00:14:46.144
I knew I was going to get here.

00:14:46.144 --> 00:14:47.117
They didn't.

00:14:47.117 --> 00:14:48.886
It was was a lot of stressful years,

00:14:48.886 --> 00:14:52.397
you know what I mean,
a lot of tough times.

00:14:52.397 --> 00:14:53.768
I proved them wrong.

00:14:53.768 --> 00:14:54.880
I proved myself right.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:58.393
- The only thing that
stops you from getting

00:14:58.393 --> 00:15:01.826
what you want in life is the bulls** story

00:15:01.826 --> 00:15:06.067
you tell yourself of
why you can't have it.

00:15:06.067 --> 00:15:06.950
You get that?

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:08.783
What stops you back is the story,

00:15:08.783 --> 00:15:11.485
'cuz the story stops
you from getting honest.

00:15:11.485 --> 00:15:14.033
If you can't get honest with yourself,

00:15:14.033 --> 00:15:14.948
there's nowhere you can go.

00:15:14.948 --> 00:15:17.501
Imagine like this,
success in sales and life,

00:15:17.501 --> 00:15:19.263
it's like a roadmap, right?

00:15:19.263 --> 00:15:21.835
You know where you want to go

00:15:21.835 --> 00:15:23.303
and you have this perfect strategy,

00:15:23.303 --> 00:15:24.660
the straight line, to get there.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:25.860
It's a perfect strategy.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.570
It's going to get you
there every single time.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:29.988
If you don't know your starting point,

00:15:29.988 --> 00:15:32.916
if you're not getting honest
with where you actually are,

00:15:32.916 --> 00:15:35.673
it doesn't matter how
powerful the strategy is

00:15:35.673 --> 00:15:37.347
and it doesn't matter how
powerful your goal is.

00:15:37.347 --> 00:15:40.506
I'm going to ask you to set
a goal today, a 60 day goal.

00:15:40.506 --> 00:15:41.990
Let's say you really set this goal.

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:43.960
I'll show you how to do
it in a brilliant way,

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:46.409
so it's visceral, so it
makes you really feel it

00:15:46.409 --> 00:15:49.042
and you see it, you sense
it, you smell the goal.

00:15:49.042 --> 00:15:50.426
That's step one.

00:15:50.426 --> 00:15:52.534
I'm going to teach you the straight line,

00:15:52.534 --> 00:15:56.160
which is your strategy
to get to your goal.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.665
If you're not honest with
where you are right now,

00:15:59.665 --> 00:16:03.165
your starting point, the map is worthless.

00:16:04.564 --> 00:16:08.389
There's three things that you
need to know: where you are,

00:16:08.389 --> 00:16:12.442
where you want to go, and how
you're going to get there.

00:16:12.442 --> 00:16:14.825
Those are the three things you must have

00:16:14.825 --> 00:16:17.969
to take advantage of any opportunity.

00:16:17.969 --> 00:16:19.374
I'm going to give you the strategy.

00:16:19.374 --> 00:16:20.830
I'm going to ask you to tell me exactly

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.747
where you want to go, for yourself.

00:16:24.988 --> 00:16:25.906
You got to get honest.

00:16:25.906 --> 00:16:27.125
Don't blame the boss.

00:16:27.125 --> 00:16:27.958
Don't blame the leagues.

00:16:27.958 --> 00:16:28.791
Don't blame your job.

00:16:28.791 --> 00:16:31.318
Don't blame the industry
you're in, just get honest.

00:16:31.318 --> 00:16:33.369
If you don't like your
industry, find another one.

00:16:33.369 --> 00:16:36.576
- You don't have to compromise yourself.

00:16:36.576 --> 00:16:38.295
If it's something that
you don't feel good about,

00:16:38.295 --> 00:16:39.128
then don't do it.

00:16:39.128 --> 00:16:43.176
The most important choices
I've made, was to say no,

00:16:43.176 --> 00:16:47.782
and I said no many a time
to films that I just didn't,

00:16:47.782 --> 00:16:51.499
especially early on, I just
didn't feel comfortable with.

00:16:51.499 --> 00:16:54.612
There was one script that was
brought to me, I called it,

00:16:54.612 --> 00:16:55.900
The Nigger They Couldn't Kill.

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:58.795
(laughter)

00:16:58.795 --> 00:17:00.837
(laughter drowns out words)

00:17:00.837 --> 00:17:04.857
He was accused of raping
this white woman, in the 40s,

00:17:04.857 --> 00:17:09.385
and they tried to hang
him, but he didn't die,

00:17:09.385 --> 00:17:11.733
and then they tried to electrocute him.

00:17:11.733 --> 00:17:12.810
They were like, "It's a comedy."

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.198
I'm like, "It ain't funny to me."

00:17:14.198 --> 00:17:15.597
(laughter)

00:17:15.597 --> 00:17:17.278
It ain't funny to me.

00:17:17.278 --> 00:17:19.636
I actually called Sidney Poitier,

00:17:19.636 --> 00:17:21.451
who I was fortunate at that time,

00:17:21.451 --> 00:17:24.278
and still, to be able to call.

00:17:24.278 --> 00:17:27.099
I said, "This movie, I'm sick,

00:17:27.099 --> 00:17:29.432
and they offered me $600,000

00:17:30.389 --> 00:17:33.468
to play the nigger they couldn't kill."

00:17:33.468 --> 00:17:34.885
That's what I call it.

00:17:34.885 --> 00:17:37.775
(laughter drowns out words)

00:17:37.775 --> 00:17:41.255
He said to me, and I'll
say this to you, he said,

00:17:41.255 --> 00:17:43.495
"The first two or three or four films

00:17:43.495 --> 00:17:45.278
you make in this industry, Denzel,

00:17:45.278 --> 00:17:47.553
will determine how you're received."

00:17:47.553 --> 00:17:50.368
He said, "I'm not going
to tell you what to do,

00:17:50.368 --> 00:17:52.623
but remember that the first three or four,

00:17:52.623 --> 00:17:55.787
five films you make will
determine how you're received."

00:17:55.787 --> 00:17:57.215
I turned it down.

00:17:57.215 --> 00:17:58.287
I turned the money down.

00:17:58.287 --> 00:18:00.026
I needed the money.

00:18:00.026 --> 00:18:00.862
I turned it down.

00:18:00.862 --> 00:18:03.420
Six months later I got Cry of Freedom.

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:06.844
(cheering and applause)

00:18:06.844 --> 00:18:08.338
So, stick to your guns.

00:18:08.338 --> 00:18:13.090
If you don't feel like you
should do it, then don't do it.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:14.794
You don't want to be,

00:18:14.794 --> 00:18:17.750
you don't want to be a
negative energy on the set.

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:19.287
That's how I feel sometimes.

00:18:19.287 --> 00:18:20.208
You know, I ain't doing this

00:18:20.208 --> 00:18:22.098
because I'm going to slap
somebody on the second day.

00:18:22.098 --> 00:18:23.461
(laughter)

00:18:23.461 --> 00:18:25.894
So I just, you know,

00:18:25.894 --> 00:18:27.796
I think the most important
decisions you can make

00:18:27.796 --> 00:18:31.756
as an actor, actress, is
saying no, is saying no.

00:18:31.756 --> 00:18:34.779
You don't have to take your clothes off.

00:18:34.779 --> 00:18:37.376
If you don't want to, then don't do it.

00:18:37.376 --> 00:18:38.376
- I love me.

00:18:40.176 --> 00:18:42.799
The day that you decide to stop loving me,

00:18:42.799 --> 00:18:46.113
I'm not going to love myself any less.

00:18:46.113 --> 00:18:47.779
I believe in me.

00:18:47.779 --> 00:18:50.457
If you stop believing in me,

00:18:50.457 --> 00:18:54.148
I'm not going to believe
in myself any less.

00:18:54.148 --> 00:18:56.822
If you believe that I'm irrelevant,

00:18:56.822 --> 00:18:58.814
that no one is checking for me,

00:18:58.814 --> 00:19:01.001
and that I don't mean
anything to the world,

00:19:01.001 --> 00:19:03.983
because you think or
believe that about me,

00:19:03.983 --> 00:19:08.791
it doesn't mean that I'm going
to believe it about myself.

00:19:08.791 --> 00:19:12.257
See, the day that you
start living your life

00:19:12.257 --> 00:19:15.799
according to everybody else's opinion

00:19:15.799 --> 00:19:17.971
is the beginning of the end.

00:19:17.971 --> 00:19:22.434
Most of you all, and it's
f**ked up, I see it every day,

00:19:22.434 --> 00:19:24.517
all day, most of you guys

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.842
don't actually know your self worth.

00:19:28.842 --> 00:19:31.441
You don't know your self value.

00:19:31.441 --> 00:19:35.608
You're like a vulnerable
little child and you're shaking

00:19:36.709 --> 00:19:39.664
and it's like everybody loves me this week

00:19:39.664 --> 00:19:42.253
so I love me this week.

00:19:42.253 --> 00:19:43.836
Next week it drops.

00:19:45.269 --> 00:19:47.838
Now you're running around insecure,

00:19:47.838 --> 00:19:50.957
feeling self-conscious,
and not loving yourself,

00:19:50.957 --> 00:19:54.448
sad and depressed, based on the feedback,

00:19:54.448 --> 00:19:56.320
the responses, and the energy

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:59.376
that the rest of the world is giving you.

00:19:59.376 --> 00:20:01.616
I wrote about this in my
new book, which is coming.

00:20:01.616 --> 00:20:03.533
It's called Black Rose.

00:20:04.692 --> 00:20:07.475
It hasn't been released
yet, but it's coming.

00:20:07.475 --> 00:20:12.003
I talk about the fact
that fame is an addiction.

00:20:12.003 --> 00:20:16.367
Fame is one of the most
unspoken addictions out there.

00:20:16.367 --> 00:20:19.260
So many celebrities and entertainers,

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.984
athletes and public figures,

00:20:21.984 --> 00:20:26.522
they base their self
worth on their relevancy,

00:20:26.522 --> 00:20:29.628
based on everybody in the
world checking for them.

00:20:29.628 --> 00:20:32.004
As soon as people stop checking for them,

00:20:32.004 --> 00:20:35.175
then they stop checking for theirself.

00:20:35.175 --> 00:20:37.161
You all don't love me no more?

00:20:37.161 --> 00:20:38.736
I'm not selling records?

00:20:38.736 --> 00:20:41.286
I'm not number one in
the box office no more?

00:20:41.286 --> 00:20:44.493
I'm not making as much
money as I used to make?

00:20:44.493 --> 00:20:45.669
Oh s**t.

00:20:45.669 --> 00:20:47.716
Ain't nobody checking for me.

00:20:47.716 --> 00:20:48.905
Guess what?

00:20:48.905 --> 00:20:51.927
I'm not checking for myself.

00:20:51.927 --> 00:20:55.464
No one sees the value in me anymore,

00:20:55.464 --> 00:20:58.110
so I don't see the value in me anymore.

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:00.642
Every time I go on Twitter, Facebook,

00:21:00.642 --> 00:21:04.809
they say I'm irrelevant, so
I'm irrelevant to myself now.

00:21:05.676 --> 00:21:09.759
I ain't s**t because you
think that I ain't s**t.

00:21:10.878 --> 00:21:12.459
No one loves me.

00:21:12.459 --> 00:21:16.675
Because you said no one
loves me, I don't love me.

00:21:16.675 --> 00:21:20.842
The day that you allow the
opinions of the outside world

00:21:21.762 --> 00:21:25.608
to dictate the way you
feel about yourself,

00:21:25.608 --> 00:21:27.347
it is the beginning of the end

00:21:27.347 --> 00:21:31.514
of you living a blessed and
self-loving, secure life.

00:21:33.719 --> 00:21:36.909
I can tell you all right
now that it is not the car

00:21:36.909 --> 00:21:39.671
that I drive or any of
the jewelry that I own

00:21:39.671 --> 00:21:44.318
or the size of my house
that defines my self-worth.

00:21:44.318 --> 00:21:45.485
M*F*, I'm hot.

00:21:47.109 --> 00:21:48.603
I'm hot.

00:21:48.603 --> 00:21:51.227
I'm hot when you don't think I'm hot.

00:21:51.227 --> 00:21:54.391
I'm amazing when you
don't think I'm amazing.

00:21:54.391 --> 00:21:57.771
I love me even if you stop loving me.

00:21:57.771 --> 00:22:00.448
You can say the nastiest, meanest,

00:22:00.448 --> 00:22:03.131
evilest s**t you could ever conjure up.

00:22:03.131 --> 00:22:07.214
It will never change the
way I feel about myself.

00:22:08.109 --> 00:22:11.259
I'm telling you, that's
the way I live my life.

00:22:11.259 --> 00:22:13.017
That's how I feel about me.

00:22:13.017 --> 00:22:17.184
Most of you all are on Twitter,
you're desperate for likes.

00:22:18.387 --> 00:22:22.660
You're desperate for the
egotistical feeding frenzy.

00:22:22.660 --> 00:22:23.873
Feed my ego.

00:22:23.873 --> 00:22:28.040
Feed, feed, feed, like me, like
me, because I don't like me.

00:22:31.639 --> 00:22:34.456
I'm telling you all right now.

00:22:34.456 --> 00:22:38.264
The day that you allow
the opinions of everybody

00:22:38.264 --> 00:22:41.564
on the outside world to
define your day to day,

00:22:41.564 --> 00:22:43.434
month to month, and year to year,

00:22:43.434 --> 00:22:45.048
it's the beginning of the end.

00:22:45.048 --> 00:22:46.597
Love yourself.

00:22:46.597 --> 00:22:48.264
Believe in yourself.

00:22:49.100 --> 00:22:49.933
Love yourself.

00:22:49.933 --> 00:22:51.455
Believe in yourself, independent

00:22:51.455 --> 00:22:54.057
of the validation of the world.

00:22:54.057 --> 00:22:56.066
Have opinions and feelings about yourself,

00:22:56.066 --> 00:22:58.399
independent of the feedback.

00:22:59.578 --> 00:23:01.695
Why you got to have somebody
calling you beautiful everyday,

00:23:01.695 --> 00:23:05.001
in order for you to feel beautiful?

00:23:05.001 --> 00:23:06.950
Do you believe that you're beautiful,

00:23:06.950 --> 00:23:08.457
or do you only believe you're beautiful

00:23:08.457 --> 00:23:11.499
when other people say
that you're beautiful?

00:23:11.499 --> 00:23:12.967
I'm just asking.

00:23:12.967 --> 00:23:16.535
Self-love is the cure to self-hate.

00:23:16.535 --> 00:23:18.271
If you make it to the end of this video

00:23:18.271 --> 00:23:22.853
I want you to write, self-love
is the cure to self-hate.

00:23:22.853 --> 00:23:24.348
These are the type of qualities

00:23:24.348 --> 00:23:27.956
that I'm going and have been
instilling in my daughter.

00:23:27.956 --> 00:23:31.478
There is no man that you
could ever meet, Shayla,

00:23:31.478 --> 00:23:33.563
that can make you feel more amazing

00:23:33.563 --> 00:23:35.888
than what you're supposed
to feel about yourself.

00:23:35.888 --> 00:23:39.219
Nobody wants to be alone,
but if you show up empty,

00:23:39.219 --> 00:23:41.963
as an empty shell, and
you're expecting this man

00:23:41.963 --> 00:23:45.090
to fulfill you and fill
you up with all of the love

00:23:45.090 --> 00:23:48.900
that doesn't exist, you're
going to be f**ked up,

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:52.400
because as soon as he leaves,
you're depleted, you're empty,

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:55.319
and you have nothing
left for yourself, again.

